---
// Shared decorative texture used on every page via Layout — kept here
// (not per-page) so Home/About/Projects all get the identical treatment
// instead of drifting apart. Two pieces:
//   1. A few large, low-contrast graphite facets for background depth
//      (grayscale only, no new hues introduced).
//   2. A dot-grid patch in two corners, fading inward via mask.
//
// This whole block is `position: absolute` and pinned to the TOP of the
// page (not `position: fixed`, and not full document height). Fixed
// positioning kept it glued to the viewport no matter how far you
// scrolled, which read as static/dead, especially on mobile. Absolute +
// capped to one screen height means it scrolls away naturally with the
// hero, like normal page content, and never stretches oddly on long
// pages (About, Projects).
---

<div class="page-texture" aria-hidden="true">
  <div class="facet facet-1"></div>
  <div class="facet facet-2"></div>
  <div class="facet facet-3"></div>
  <div class="corner-dots corner-dots--tr"></div>
  <div class="corner-dots corner-dots--bl"></div>
</div>

<style>
  .page-texture {
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    left: 0;
    right: 0;
    height: 100dvh;
    z-index: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .facet {
    position: absolute;
    opacity: 0.55;
  }

  .facet-1 {
    top: -10%;
    left: -5%;
    width: 60%;
    height: 55%;
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1e1a16, transparent 70%);
  }

  .facet-2 {
    bottom: -15%;
    right: -10%;
    width: 55%;
    height: 60%;
    background: linear-gradient(315deg, #1a1613, transparent 70%);
  }

  .facet-3 {
    top: 20%;
    right: 5%;
    width: 35%;
    height: 40%;
    background: linear-gradient(200deg, #171310, transparent 75%);
  }

  .corner-dots {
    position: absolute;
    width: 160px;
    height: 160px;
    background-image: radial-gradient(rgba(242, 237, 230, 0.3) 1.4px, transparent 1.4px);
    background-size: 14px 14px;
  }

  .corner-dots--tr {
    top: 0;
    right: 0;
    -webkit-mask-image: radial-gradient(circle at 100% 0%, black 0%, transparent 75%);
    mask-image: radial-gradient(circle at 100% 0%, black 0%, transparent 75%);
  }

  .corner-dots--bl {
    bottom: 0;
    left: 0;
    -webkit-mask-image: radial-gradient(circle at 0% 100%, black 0%, transparent 75%);
    mask-image: radial-gradient(circle at 0% 100%, black 0%, transparent 75%);
  }
</style>
